| 13b | WAVE TWO, ahead of rank 16 | `K3` the restore drill at one revision: `tools/census-drill.mjs` stands as the drill (exporter and importer at one revision, a keep with one flipped byte refusing before any import); the crossing's burn left export, import, the bundle format, the keep and the census standing, the parity witness already reading one revision with no stand-off flag or moved class, and its census, compare and `--base` standing for the drill; the drill knows the bundle's skipped kāpae marks and reads face canon on both sides, and the compare takes each census file the card names (the two known red shapes and the card's glob of rank 4f); `K4` the keep names its revision and a kūkulu's landing owes a keep (`packages/lares-cli/src/rite-keep-host.ts`); design lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/evergreen-keep #/the-plan. The keep's-restore rename stands (PR #232, `f694aedf4`), and a restore refuses an unsigned roster before any door (PR #289); the drill stays unwalked against a real keep, and census-drill P2 refuses at `persona new 1` with `face-not-lent` before any bundle code runs (PR #259's cold read). The old house's burn waits on this drill (operator, 2026-11-18, the defaults in the decisions row): `~/.lares-prior` and `lares-surface:pre-carry` burn after one keep restore drill reads `par` on the operator's house and `docker ps -a --filter ancestor=lares-surface:pre-carry` reads empty before the image goes (backlog-alpha #/next). Holder: Lares-Alpha (backlog-alpha #/next) | The drill walks the one restore path the keep owes, and a keep that names its revision lets a restore read the cut's own code. |

